## 🚀 Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/F1SMV/Neural-DX-Watcher.git
cd Neural-DX-Watcher
chmod +x start.sh
./start.sh
```

Available at `http://localhost:8000`

> 💡 A **Raspberry Pi** is recommended for its low power consumption, but the program runs on any Linux PC.

---

## ⚙️ Technical Architecture

- Backend: Python / Flask
- Frontend: HTML / CSS / JavaScript
- Cluster: Telnet DX Cluster
- Analysis: dedicated Python scripts (`predictor.py`, `dxcc_resolver.py`)
- Storage: memory + local JSON + **SQLite**

No cloud dependency.

---

## 🗂️ Version History

### v11.2 — Critical Fixes: META ANALYSIS, AI Insight, Satellites

#### 🐛 500 Error on META ANALYSIS — Missing Analyzer Script

The `tools/` directory and `tools/log_meta_analyzer.py` script simply didn't exist on the server — the `POST /api/meta/run` route was failing systematically. Complete rewrite of the missing script:

- Parses `SPOT: CALL (band, mode) -> SPD: X pts (Dist: Ykm)` lines from the application log
- Deduplicates by callsign (keeps best SPD score), sorts top spots
- Generates `data/meta/summary.json` in the exact format expected by the AI Insight page
- Designed to never crash: missing or empty log → valid empty summary, never an error

Additionally, the backend now returns the **actual error detail** (script `stderr`) instead of a bare opaque return code — future errors will be immediately diagnosable instead of requiring blind investigation.

#### 🔧 AI Insight Page — Native `confirm()`/`alert()` Finally Replaced

The `analysis.html` → `ai_insight.html` rename (v10.2) had carried over a version predating the dialog fixes made along the way — native browser popups (`confirm()`, `alert()`) were still present in production. Fixed: inline HTML dialog for run confirmation, detailed error message (including backend `stderr`) displayed directly on the page.

#### ⏳ Satellites Page — Loading Indicator

The first position computation call (TLE + sgp4) can take up to 45 seconds after a server restart. Added an explicit loading indicator (animated hourglass + message) on the map, automatically removed once positions arrive.

#### 📡 Index Page — Clarified Wait Message

The spot table showed a generic empty message without explaining that the DX Cluster feed is **real-time** (no backlog on connection) — a new spot must literally happen somewhere after your connection to appear. Message replaced with a clear explanation of this normal behavior.

#### 🎨 "WHO HEARS ME" Toggle — Color Adjusted

The reception envelope line changes from dark green to **red**, significantly more visible against the Esri satellite map background.

