### v11.1 — Security Level 2 · "WHO HEARS ME" Toggle on HF & VHF/UHF Maps

#### 🔒 Security Level 2 — Local API Token

- Hex token auto-generated on first startup, persisted to `data/api_token.txt` (`chmod 600`)
- `@require_api_token` decorator on state-modifying routes: `/update_qra`, `/spot`, `/api/spot`, `/watchlist.json` (POST/DELETE only — `GET` stays open, read continuously by all 3 modes), `/api/briefing/refresh`, `/api/lotw/login`, `/api/lotw/logout`, `/api/satellites/config`, `/api/satellites/refresh_tle`, `/api/ntfy/test`
- New `GET /api/token` route distributes the token to the frontend
- **Global `fetch()` interceptor** on the frontend (`index.html`, `satellites.html`, `map.html`, `ai_insight.html`): every `POST`/`DELETE` request automatically receives the `X-API-Token` header, without patching hundreds of individual calls
- Fixed bug: a function registered under two routes (`/spot` + `/api/spot`) with a duplicated `@require_api_token` caused a Flask `AssertionError` at startup — a single decorator placed right above `def` resolves the endpoint conflict

#### 📶 "WHO HEARS ME" Toggle — Real Coverage Visualization on Maps

New feature leveraging data already collected by MY SIGNAL: a **`📶 QUI M'ENTEND`** button on both maps (**DX MAP HF** and **DX MAP VHF/UHF**), visualizing at a glance who's actually receiving the signal, in which direction, and how far.

**Behavior**:
- Hides regular DX spots while active (map too crowded otherwise)
- Draws a **closed envelope** connecting **all** stations receiving you, sorted by bearing from the QTH — a real continuous reception diagram, not a star radiating from the center
- Solid line (no dashes), dark green, clearly visible
- Triangular markers color-coded by SNR (green ≥-5dB, yellow -15 to -5dB, red <-15dB), farthest station highlighted (🎯)
- Strict HF / VHF-UHF separation: a 6m spot only shows on the HF map, a 2m/70cm spot only on the VHF/UHF map (same split as `HF_BANDS`/`VHF_BANDS` on the backend) — new `band` field added to the `/api/my-signal` response (via the existing `find_band()`)
- **"always · stations hearing me"** checkbox — persisted in `localStorage`, automatically restores the display on every page load
- Main refresh every 3 minutes + lightweight check every 15s comparing a signature of the currently received station set (call + band + timestamp): any change (new station, band switch mid-operation) triggers an immediate recalculation without waiting for the full cycle

**Bugs fixed along the way**:
- The periodic regular-spot refresh (`updateMaps()`) unconditionally re-attached markers to the map, undoing the requested hide — now gated on toggle state
- Reference to a variable removed during the HF/VHF refactor (`mySignalOn`) causing a silent JS error every 90s cycle — cleaned up
- Visual overlap of the button with the panel title (`float:right` on a non-flex header) — fixed with flexbox `justify-content:space-between`

#### 🎨 Visual Adjustments

- Enlarged MY SIGNAL panel labels (callsign, mode/frequency, distance, SNR badge)
- Max reported distance highlighted: 1.35× size, orange, bold
- Green border highlight on reports with SNR > 0dB, significantly strengthened (opacity, border thickness)
- Classic/smart layout column widths adjusted: center column (maps) widened by 1cm, side columns reduced by 0.5cm each — better readability for maps and their new reception diagrams

---

### v11.0 — Genuinely Measured Predictive Engine (Complete Rewrite) · Hardened Security

#### 🧠 Complete Rewrite of `predictor.py`

Moving from unmeasured manual coefficients to a truly **self-evaluating** engine:

**New `dxcc_resolver.py` module** — unified DXCC resolution based on the `cty.dat` file already used by the rest of the application. Handles a callsign (`"DL9XYZ/P"`), a prefix (`"DL"`), or a DXCC entity name (`"Germany"`) indiscriminately — fixes a serious bug where `_extract_prefix()` blindly cut the first 3 characters of whatever value it received, including a country name coming from LoTW (`"Germany"` became `"GER"` instead of the correct prefix `"DL"`), silently breaking the prediction engine's directional coefficients.
- Robust `cty.dat` parser: handles prefix ranges (`D40-D49`, `D3A-D3Z` via expansion), exact callsign overrides (`=CALL`), tolerant substring-word fallback for LoTW's short-name variants vs cty.dat's formal names
- Safe degraded mode if `cty.dat` is missing — the app never crashes, it only loses directional precision

**4 distinct propagation models** based on band, instead of a single generic model:
- **Es** model (6m): seasonal/hourly patterns + directional boost per prefix + Kp degradation
- **HF** model: ionospheric, SFI/Kp dependency per band + day/night preference
- **Tropo** model (2m/4m/70cm/23cm): dawn/dusk bonus + summer seasonal boost
- **TEP** (trans-equatorial) boost, stackable on eligible bands (6m/10m/15m) during evening near equinoxes

**Prediction self-verification**: every prediction issued is logged into a new `prediction_log` table (deduplicated by band/prefix/time-slot), then automatically compared against actually received spots once its window has elapsed (new `verify_predictions()` method, called every 30 minutes from the existing maintenance worker).

**Measured reliability displayed**: the cockpit "🔮 PERSONALIZED PREDICTIONS" panel now shows a banner `📊 Measured reliability: 72% over 30 days — 18 observations` (color-coded green/orange/red based on the rate), with per-model breakdown available (Es/HF/tropo). While history is still insufficient, it explicitly shows "not enough history yet" rather than a made-up number. Per-prediction model badge (Es cyan / HF orange / Tropo purple).

**Empirical Bayesian smoothing**: the final probability blends the model's theoretical score with the actually observed rate in history for a comparable bin (same band, UTC hour ±1h, month ±1, direction/prefix) — the richer the available history, the closer the score gets to measured reality. A `solar_log` table and a `record_solar_sample()` method are prepared (not automatically wired) for a future v12 that could refine this smoothing with real SFI/Kp history.

**Safe database migration**: existing v10 `predictor.sqlite` databases (missing the `prefix` column) are automatically migrated at startup without data loss.

#### 🔒 Security and Hygiene

- `debug=False` in `app.run()` — the interactive Werkzeug debugger in debug mode exposed arbitrary code execution on the local network if an unhandled exception occurred, a critical vulnerability even in home use
- LoTW export files (containing the entire contact log) moved from `/tmp` (readable by all system users) to `data/` (private, already excluded from Git), with restricted `chmod 600` permissions
- `start.sh` rewritten: clean shutdown via `SIGTERM` (5s wait) before `kill -9` as a last resort only; dependency installation is now **conditional** — a quick test checks whether everything is already available before running `pip install`, using `requirements.txt` if present, avoiding a systematic network call on every startup

---

### v10.5 — Theory vs Reality · MY SIGNAL (PSK Reporter Self-monitoring)

#### 🔬 Theory vs Reality — VOACAP × Actual Spots Crossover

The cockpit VOACAP table now offers a **3-view toggle** in its header:

- **THEORY**: theoretical VOACAP prediction computed from SFI/Kp/zone (original behavior)
- **REAL**: intensity of spots actually observed over the last 24 hours, aggregated by band × 3h slot × continental zone (EU/NA/AS/OC/AF/SA detected via DXCC prefix)
- **Δ DELTA**: actual − theoretical gap. Green = unpredicted opening (Es/TEP/aurora); red = dead band despite favorable prediction

New backend route: `GET /api/reality-check/<zone>` — queries the predictor's `spot_log` SQLite table, normalizes to relative intensity (0-100%) over the max across all bands/slots. Bilingual FR/EN orange legend below the table.

#### 📶 MY SIGNAL — PSK Reporter Self-monitoring

New **"📶 MY SIGNAL"** panel — who's hearing you, where, with what SNR, without ever leaving the application.

- New backend route `GET /api/my-signal`: queries the PSK Reporter API (`retrieve.pskreporter.info/query`) via **JSONP** (`callback=cb` parameter — `format=json` does NOT work with this API, returns a silent error), extracts the JSON by stripping the `cb(...)` wrapper via regex
- 90-second server cache (respects PSK Reporter's usage policy, which recommends no more than 1 query per minute)
- All bands HF/VHF/UHF, all digital modes (FT8/FT4/WSPR/JT65/JS8/MSK144)
- Display: receiver callsign, mode, frequency, computed distance (via cty.dat/Maidenhead), report age, color-coded SNR (green ≥-5dB / yellow -15 to -5dB / red <-15dB), header summary
- Integrated in **all 3 modes**: CLASSIC and SMART (column 3) and COCKPIT (column 3) — a single JS function populates both locations in one fetch
- Limited to 20 displayed stations

#### 🔧 WSJT-X Fixes

The spot injection filter (CQ only + stations calling me directly) was tested without filtering (inject everything) but proved unusable in practice, the original filter was restored with an additional anti-self-spot guard.

> v10.4 was an internal working version, never published — its features were absorbed into v10.5.

